        "completedSourceTexts": [
          {
            "textId": "completed:paper-mock-anhui-jiangnan10-2025-m1:seven-choices:3",
            "paragraphId": "block:paper-mock-anhui-jiangnan10-2025-m1:seven-choices:3",
            "text": "It may sound simple, but it’s effective. Staying connected can go a long way toward managing your depression. This reminds you that you’re not alone. According to research, increased social connection and feeling connected can help decrease depressive symptoms."
          },
          {
            "textId": "completed:paper-mock-anhui-jiangnan10-2025-m1:seven-choices:5",
            "paragraphId": "block:paper-mock-anhui-jiangnan10-2025-m1:seven-choices:5",
            "text": "Depression can surface through a lot of negative thoughts, but you can learn how to challenge them with know-how and effort. This doesn’t mean just telling yourself everything’s fine. Rather, it’s a way to look at your real situation and restore your positivity. For instance, you might remind yourself that you are loved and then give specific examples to support this new thought pattern."
          },
          {
            "textId": "completed:paper-mock-anhui-jiangnan10-2025-m1:seven-choices:7",
            "paragraphId": "block:paper-mock-anhui-jiangnan10-2025-m1:seven-choices:7",
            "text": "Engaging in rewarding activities can help you stay active and out of depression. This can involve scheduled activities of mental health strategies. For example, you can start your day with positive self-talk and end it by writing down something you are grateful for. Including these activities into your routine can help with depression."
          },
          {
            "textId": "completed:paper-mock-anhui-jiangnan10-2025-m1:seven-choices:9",
            "paragraphId": "block:paper-mock-anhui-jiangnan10-2025-m1:seven-choices:9",
            "text": "When you’re struggling with depression, it can be difficult to be grateful. However, being appreciative has mental health benefits. Focusing on gratitude can bring you an increased sense of well-being, and help you transform your understanding of belongings and abilities into sources of gratitude."
          },
          {
            "textId": "completed:paper-mock-anhui-jiangnan10-2025-m1:seven-choices:10",
            "paragraphId": "block:paper-mock-anhui-jiangnan10-2025-m1:seven-choices:10",
            "text": "Learn to accept it"
          }
